  "distractor_rules": {
    "roots": [
      "The three labels are fixed as past, present, future. Never change them or their order.",
      "Every stem must be clearly one tense. No stem may be read two ways.",
      "Keep the pool near equal past, present, and future.",
      "Past uses irregular or -ed verbs and may use yesterday, last, or earlier.",
      "Present uses am, is, or are plus -ing, or simple present forms such as goes, purrs, or smiles.",
      "Future uses will plus a base verb and may use later, soon, tonight, or tomorrow.",
      "Never use going to for future, because it can look like present progressive.",
      "Never use real names. Use <NAME> only.",
      "Stems stay in kid world: school, home, food, pets, play, family, weather. No brands.",
      "For tier 3, use near misses: will plus a base verb that looks present, or yesterday plus an irregular past."
    ]
  },
